# Union merge for append-only ledgers: when two branches each add an entry,
# Git keeps both sides' lines instead of writing conflict markers. Union never
# reports a conflict, so it also keeps both versions of a line two branches
# edited in place. `npm run agents:check` fails on a repeated ticket heading.
#
# Only these two files qualify. Do not add the other ledgers:
# - STATUS.md has a table edited in place, and scripts/archive-status.mjs
#   removes blocks; union would bring archived entries back.
# - docs/MESSAGING_CHANGES.md and docs/LEGAL.md have single-line "is next"
#   counters and index tables; union would keep both counter values.
#
# tests/check-agents-ledger.test.mjs proves it for local `git merge` and
# `git rebase`. Whether
# GitHub's server-side merge honours it has not been verified.
docs/TICKETS.md merge=union
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=union
